  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the shore of Lake Sainte-Croix, in Bauduen, this rental operator offers kayaks and paddleboards to explore the lake's turquoise waters, with the cliffs plunging into the water as a backdrop.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>This page does not refer to a single operator. In Bauduen, the Lacs et Gorges du Verdon tourist office says "animals accepted" and "animals kept on a leash" for Playa Location, and "animals accepted on a leash only" for the Centre nautique de Bauduen. The Playa Location website also says "animals accepted on a leash" and offers kayaks, paddleboards, canoes, pedal boats and electric boats. The pages read do not specify whether the dog may board a kayak or paddleboard: ask the operator directly this rule before you travel.</p>
      <p>Playa Location (rue des Jardins, beach side) gives on its website hours that vary with the season: April, May and October from 10am to 6pm, closed on Tuesday and Wednesday; June and September every day from 9am to 6pm; July and August every day from 9am to 7pm, weather permitting. Bookings are made on the website (at least 24 hours in advance), by phone on 06 72 01 60 43 or on site; a snack bar with a shaded terrace and several free car parks are mentioned nearby. The tourist office page announces opening from 1 April to 30 September, which differs from the operator's website for October.</p>
      <p>The Centre nautique de Bauduen (Les Aires district, 04 94 70 09 22) is a sailing school that also rents canoe-kayaks and paddleboards; the tourist office gives 9am to 7pm in summer and variable hours out of season, posted at the entrance of the base, with a minimum age of 6 for customers. The electric boat rental company Alize Electronic Location, also in Bauduen, specifies on the tourist office page that dogs are accepted, the customer remaining responsible for damage to the equipment.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call before you come to confirm availability and the conditions for your dog, especially in high season.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Lake Sainte-Croix and the Verdon Gorges are right next door, to extend the outing on the water or on foot.</p>
